          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em weak factorization system
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{L},\mathcal{R})
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classes"} classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+morphisms"}> projective morphisms
            ” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"}> injective morphisms
            ”) such that 1) every morphism of the category factors as the composite of one in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
            followed by one in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
            are closed under having the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
            against each other.
          %p
            If the liftings here are unique, then one speaks of an
            = succeed "." do
              %em orthogonal factorization system
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28epi%2Cmono%29-factorization+system"} (epi,mono)-factorization system
            on the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            or in fact on any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %p
            Non-orthogonal weak factorization systems are the key ingredient in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R} =
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R} =
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
          %p
            There are other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properties"} properties
            which one may find or impose on a weak factorization system, for instance
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            which one may find or impose, such as for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+weak+factorization+systems"} algebraic weak factorization systems
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} factorization system
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#weak_factorization_systems Weak factorization systems
          #WeakFactorizationSystem.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong weak factorization system
              (WFS) on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{L},\mathcal{R})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classes"} classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X\to Y
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  may be factored as the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  of a morphism in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℒ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
                  followed by one in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℛ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℒ
                        %mi Z
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℛ
                        %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f\;\colon\;  X \overset{\in \mathcal{L}}{\longrightarrow} Z \overset{\in \mathcal{R}}{\longrightarrow} Y
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  The classes are closed under having the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
                  against each other:
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℒ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
                      is precisely the class of morphisms having the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                      against every morphism in
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi ℛ
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℛ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
                      is precisely the class of morphisms having the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                      against every morphism in
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi ℒ
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
          #FunctorialFactorization.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
              of the morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi fact
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    fact \;\colon\; \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]}
            %p
              which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_1 \;\colon \;\mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]}\to \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorialFactorization"}
              we are using the following notation, see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              and at
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+of+a+category"} nerve of a category
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1] = \{0 \to 1\}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[2] = \{0 \to 1 \to 2\}
              for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+numbers"} ordinal numbers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
              and hence as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(\mathcal{C})
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]} \coloneqq Funct(\Delta[1], \mathcal{C})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Funct
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]}\coloneqq Funct(\Delta[2], \mathcal{C})
              has as objects pairs of composable morphisms in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i \colon [1] \rightarrow [2]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i
              omits the index
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              in its image. By precomposition, this induces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i  \colon \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[2]} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_1
                  sends a pair of composable morphisms to their
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_2
                  sends a pair of composable morphisms to the first morphism;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0
                  sends a pair of composable morphisms to the second morphism.
          #FunctorialWeakFactorizationSystem.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A weak factorization system, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakFactorizationSystem"}
              %strong functorial weak factorization system
              if the factorization of morphisms may be chosen to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi fact
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fact
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorialFactorization"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi fact
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_2 \circ fact
              lands in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi fact
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_0\circ fact
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℛ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Not all weak factorization systems are functorial, although most (including those produced by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+systems"} orthogonal factorization systems
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrthogonalFactorizationSystem"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0106152"} Isaksen 2001
          %h3#orthogonal_factorization_systems Orthogonal factorization systems
          #OrthogonalFactorizationSystem.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"} orthogonal factorization system
              (OFS) is a weak factorization system
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℛ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{L},\mathcal{R})
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakFactorizationSystem"}
              such that the lifts of elements in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              against elements in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %em unique
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              While every OFS (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrthogonalFactorizationSystem"}
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakFactorizationSystem"}
            %p
              A “basic example” of an OFS is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28epi%2Cmono%29-factorization"} (epi,mono)-factorization
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              (meaning
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is the collection of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              that of
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %p
              The OFS (epi, mono) generalizes to any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
              if we replace “epi” with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
              if we instead replace “mono” with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular mono
            %p
              On the other hand, saying that (mono,epi) is a WFS in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is equivalent to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,R)
              is a WFS, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is the class of inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\hookrightarrow A\sqcup B
              into a binary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is the class of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} split epis
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system+on+Set"} weak factorization system on Set
          %h3#algebraic_weak_factorization_systems Algebraic weak factorization systems
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+weak+factorization+system"} algebraic weak factorization system
            enhances the
            %em properties
            of lifting and factorization to algebraic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} structure
          %h3#accessible_weak_factorization_systems Accessible weak factorization systems
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+weak+factorization+system"} accessible weak factorization system
            is a wfs on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            whose factorization is given by an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible functor
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ClosureProperties Closure properties
          #ClosuredPropertiesOfWeakFactorizationSystem.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{L},\mathcal{R})
              be a weak factorization system, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakFactorizationSystem"}
              on some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Both classes contain the class of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  Both classes are closed under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℒ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
                  is also closed under
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              %li
                %p
                  Both classes are closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
                  (see remark
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfMorphisms"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℒ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
                  of morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  (“
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobase+change"}> cobase change
                  ”).
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℛ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  of morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  (“
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"}> base change
                  ”).
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℒ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℛ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p We go through each item in turn.
            %p
              %strong containing isomorphisms
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Iso
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{f}{\rightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}_{\mathllap{\in Iso}}^{\mathllap{i}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              with the left morphism an isomorphism, then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
              is given by using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
              of this isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∘
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                      %mo ↗
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{{f \circ i^{-1}}}\nearrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathcal{R}
              and so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathcal{L}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
            %p
              %strong closure under composition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℒ
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in \mathcal{L}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              consider its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              decomposition as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℒ
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;\searrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in \mathcal{L}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now the bottom commuting square has a lift, by assumption. This yields another
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              decomposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℒ
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in \mathcal{L}}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              and now the top commuting square has a lift by assumption. This is now equivalently a lift in the total diagram, showing that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1\circ p_1
              has the right lifting property against
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              and is hence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℛ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              follows since the latter is given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              of sequential composition and successive lifts against the underlying sequence as above constitutes a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            %p
              %strong closure under retracts
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of an
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathcal{L}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℒ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    id_A \colon &amp; A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{L}}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}}
                    \\\
                    id_B \colon &amp; B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; D &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Then for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{j}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              composite with that retract diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℒ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{L}}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; D &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Now the pasting composite of the two squares on the right has a lift, by assumption,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℒ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{L}}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\nearrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; D &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By composition, this is also a lift in the total outer rectangle, hence in the original square. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              has the left lifting property against all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathcal{R}
              and hence is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formally dual
            %p
              %strong closure under pushout and pullback
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathcal{R}
              and and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Z \times_f X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{{f^* p}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    Z &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* p
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              with respect to all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathcal{L}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℒ
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi f
                                      %mo *
                                    %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Z \times_f X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in \mathcal{L}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mathrlap{f^* p}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Z
                    }
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              composite with the pullback square from above to obtain the commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Z \times_f X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f^* p}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Z &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the right lifting property of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}} &amp;{}^{\hat {(f g)}}\nearrow&amp;  \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{f g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              this gives rise to the lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat g
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; Z \times_f X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp;{}^{\hat g} \nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f^* p}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Z &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              In order for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat g
              to qualify as the intended lift of the total diagram, it remains to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Z \times_f X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}} &amp; {}^{\hat g}\nearrow
                    \\\
                    B
                    }
            %p
              commutes. To do so we notice that we obtain two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
              with tip
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %ul
              %li
                %p one is given by the morphisms
                %ol
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo →
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to Z \times_f X \to X
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                          %mi Z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{g}{\to} Z
                %p with universal morphism into the pullback being
                %ul
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo →
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to Z \times_f X
              %li
                %p the other by
                %ol
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{\hat g}{\to} Z \times_f X \to X
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                          %mi Z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{g}{\to} Z
                    \.
                %p with universal morphism into the pullback being
                %ul
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{\hat g}{\to} Z \times_f X
                    \.
            %p
              The commutativity of the diagrams that we have established so far shows that the first and second morphisms here equal each other, respectively. By the fact that the universal morphism into a pullback diagram is
              %em unique
              this implies the required identity of morphisms.
            %p
              The other case is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
            %p
              %strong closure under (co-)products
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi s
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(A_s \overset{i_s}{\to} B_s) \in \mathcal{L}\}_{s \in S}
              be a set of elements of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              are computed componentwise, their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              is the universal morphism out of the coproduct of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{s \in S}{\coprod} A_s
              induced via its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              by the set of morphisms
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_s
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi s
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi s
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi S
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} A_s
                    \\overset{(i_s)_{s\in S}}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} B_s
                    \\,.
            %p Now let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi s
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi s
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(i_s)_{s\in S}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of objects, hence by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the coproduct, this is equivalent to a set of commuting diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi A
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi ℒ
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi s
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi ℛ
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi f
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i_s}}_{\mathllap{\in \mathcal{L}}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\right\}_{s\in S}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By assumption, each of these has a lift
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_s
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi A
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi ℒ
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi s
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ℓ
                                      %mi s
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi ℛ
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi f
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i_s}}_{\mathllap{\in \mathcal{L}}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;{}^{\ell_s}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\right\}_{s\in S}
            %p
              is now itself a compatible
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the coproduct, this is equivalent to a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\ell_s)_{s\in S}
              in the original square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi s
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi s
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi ℓ
                                  %mi s
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi s
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi S
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi ℛ
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(i_s)_{s\in S}}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;{}^{(\ell_s)_{s\in S}}\nearrow&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in \mathcal{R}}}
                    \\\
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows that the coproduct of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_s
              has the left lifting property against all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in \mathcal{R}
              and is hence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Beware, in the situation of prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosuredPropertiesOfWeakFactorizationSystem"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              is not in general closed under all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              is not in general closed under all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              is not in general closed under forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              is not in general closed under forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℛ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{L},\mathcal{R})
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"} orthogonal factorization system
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrthogonalFactorizationSystem"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              is closed under all colimits and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              is closed under all limits.
          #RetractsOfMorphisms.num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              Here by a
              %em retract
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} Y
              in some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is meant a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as an object in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi g
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow} B
              such that in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              there is a factorization of the identity on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    id_g \;\colon\;
                    g \longrightarrow f \longrightarrow g
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means equivalently that in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    id_A \colon &amp; A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    id_B \colon &amp; B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
          %h3#retract_argument Retract argument
          #RetractArgument.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract+argument"}> retract argument
                )
            %p
              Consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi i
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi p
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; X\stackrel{i}{\longrightarrow} A \stackrel{p}{\longrightarrow} Y
                    \\,.
            %p Then:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                  against
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                  against
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We discuss the first statement, the second is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formally dual
            %p
              Write the factorization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{i}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;= &amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the assumed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              against
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              there exists a diagonal filler
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              making a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{i}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow &amp;{}^{\mathllap{g}}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;= &amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p By rearranging this diagram a little, it is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; X &amp;=&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}\downarrow
                    \\\
                    id_Y \colon &amp; Y &amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A &amp;\underset{p}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Completing this to the right, this yields a diagram exhibiting the required retract according to remark
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfMorphisms"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    id_X \colon &amp; X &amp;=&amp; X &amp;=&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow
                    \\\
                    id_Y \colon &amp; Y &amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A &amp;\underset{p}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} Model categories
                provide many examples of weak factorization systems. In fact, most applications of WFS involve model categories or model-categorical ideas.
            %li
              %p
                The existence of certain
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system+on+Set"} WFS on Set
                is related to the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %li
              %p
                See the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/joyalscatlab/published/Weak+factorisation+systems"} Catlab
                for more examples.
